`md list` prints an ABSOLUTE path in every record, and the harness runs each
case in a scratch directory whose name is random, so a line holding a path can
never be pinned byte for byte. Cases that list at least one file therefore pipe
the output through `md lines`, which selects the lines that hold no path.

run.py copies only the FILES of a case directory to the scratch directory, and
never a subdirectory, so a real nested tree cannot be staged and the recursion
itself is not tested here. What this case does guard is that -r leaves a flat
directory alone: the same two blocks and five lines, which `md lines --count`
reports as 5.
